'''''Greyia sutherlandii''''', also known as '''Natal bottlebrush''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Francoaceae]].<ref name=COL>{{cite web |url= https://www.catalogueoflife.org/data/taxon/3HDPF |title= Greyia sutherlandii Hook. & Harv. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=n.d. |website=Catalogue of Life |publisher=Species 2000 |access-date=November 29, 2024}}</ref> It is native to [[South Africa]], [[Eswatini]], and [[Lesotho]].<ref name="PoTWO">{{cite powo |title=''Greyia sutherlandii'' Hook. & Harv.|id=783197-1 |accessdate=2021-02-16}}</ref>

== Appearance ==
''Greyia sutherlandii'' is a small to medium-sized tree that can reach heights of up to 10 meters (30 feet). It has distinctive bottlebrush-like flower clusters and elliptical leaves.

